1
00:00:02,055 --> 00:00:05,427
So let's make our webpage a little bit more

2
00:00:05,555 --> 00:00:08,253
beautiful. And for that, we can add some CSS

3
00:00:08,317 --> 00:00:08,911
styling.

4
00:00:09,666 --> 00:00:11,817
For this, at Hatch, you find the app.css

5
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:12,042
file,

6
00:00:12,716 --> 00:00:15,494
which you can just drag and drop. So

7
00:00:15,510 --> 00:00:17,405
download and then drag and drop into your

8
00:00:17,453 --> 00:00:18,336
project folder.

9
00:00:19,364 --> 00:00:22,752
And here I now want to add a link to import

10
00:00:22,752 --> 00:00:24,566
this app.css file like this.

11
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:28,141
The problem is if we just do this

12
00:00:29,006 --> 00:00:31,297
and we run our application, that's not going

13
00:00:31,394 --> 00:00:31,890
to work.

14
00:00:32,627 --> 00:00:35,255
If we reload, you see it still looks the way

15
00:00:35,255 --> 00:00:35,928
it did before.

16
00:00:36,857 --> 00:00:38,924
A reason for that can be found if we open up

17
00:00:38,924 --> 00:00:39,757
the developer tools

18
00:00:40,526 --> 00:00:42,657
under network. If we reload, we see a

19
00:00:42,705 --> 00:00:45,749
failing request for app.css. It gets back

20
00:00:45,749 --> 00:00:48,730
status code 404, so it's not found.

21
00:00:49,274 --> 00:00:51,806
And the reason for that is simply that in

22
00:00:51,982 --> 00:00:54,870
our server, in our Deno server which in the

23
00:00:54,870 --> 00:00:56,681
end receives all requests,

24
00:00:57,474 --> 00:01:00,336
we got no route that would return that CSS

25
00:01:00,369 --> 00:01:00,660
file.

26
00:01:01,402 --> 00:01:03,529
Now, this does not mean that we now need to

27
00:01:03,722 --> 00:01:04,109
add a new

28
00:01:04,785 --> 00:01:05,511
GET route

29
00:01:06,477 --> 00:01:09,378
for app.css. This is not what we need to do

30
00:01:09,378 --> 00:01:09,700
here.

31
00:01:12,069 --> 00:01:13,944
We don't have to add this route

32
00:01:14,656 --> 00:01:17,614
because the CSS file, just like images and

33
00:01:17,646 --> 00:01:19,796
so on, which we might have on our page, is

34
00:01:19,829 --> 00:01:21,009
simply a static file.

35
00:01:21,602 --> 00:01:23,927
We basically want to configure our server

36
00:01:23,927 --> 00:01:27,744
such that all those requests which are sent

37
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:31,031
automatically from inside our HTML document,

38
00:01:31,448 --> 00:01:34,174
like CSS files, like JavaScript files, like

39
00:01:34,270 --> 00:01:37,300
images, that all those requests for static

40
00:01:37,397 --> 00:01:40,924
resources are just forwarded in the end and

41
00:01:40,924 --> 00:01:43,362
are just answered automatically by our

42
00:01:43,426 --> 00:01:45,013
server. That's what we want,

43
00:01:45,575 --> 00:01:47,419
and that's something we can easily implement

44
00:01:47,419 --> 00:01:48,525
here with Oak.

45
00:01:49,469 --> 00:01:52,454
Oak returns a method or a function we can

46
00:01:52,535 --> 00:01:54,939
use for that, and that's the send function.

47
00:01:55,982 --> 00:01:58,764
We can use the send function to send a file

48
00:01:58,974 --> 00:02:01,949
or send a resource in general back to the

49
00:02:01,949 --> 00:02:03,680
client when it's requested.

50
00:02:04,311 --> 00:02:06,295
And for this, we need to register a new

51
00:02:06,649 --> 00:02:07,147
middleware.

52
00:02:08,016 --> 00:02:08,611
I'll add it here,

53
00:02:10,252 --> 00:02:11,426
and this middleware

54
00:02:13,228 --> 00:02:14,659
now will basically

55
00:02:15,887 --> 00:02:16,752
call send.

56
00:02:17,729 --> 00:02:18,979
Now we get our context here

57
00:02:19,668 --> 00:02:22,439
and send returns a promise which eventually

58
00:02:22,536 --> 00:02:24,522
resolves to a string or to undefined.

59
00:02:25,179 --> 00:02:28,015
Now send also wants an argument.

60
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,546
It essentially needs to get access to the

61
00:02:30,546 --> 00:02:33,254
request and the response passed in one

62
00:02:33,510 --> 00:02:35,818
object which contains both request and

63
00:02:35,850 --> 00:02:36,314
response.

64
00:02:37,212 --> 00:02:39,935
Now we got such an object, the context. It

65
00:02:39,935 --> 00:02:42,563
has access to both request and response so

66
00:02:42,563 --> 00:02:44,951
we can just forward the context to send.

67
00:02:46,268 --> 00:02:48,436
But send wants more. It does not just want

68
00:02:48,436 --> 00:02:51,182
this object, it also wants to know for which

69
00:02:51,407 --> 00:02:54,346
path we should send back a response.

70
00:02:55,021 --> 00:02:57,333
So the second argument here will be the

71
00:02:57,333 --> 00:03:00,786
context request, and there the URL object,

72
00:03:00,866 --> 00:03:02,970
and there the path name. That's the

73
00:03:02,970 --> 00:03:05,877
requested resource path in the end. So for

74
00:03:05,877 --> 00:03:08,816
the CSS file, this would essentially be— so

75
00:03:08,816 --> 00:03:10,807
for this file here, this would essentially

76
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:11,305
be

77
00:03:13,652 --> 00:03:15,638
/app.css. That would be the path name here.

78
00:03:17,010 --> 00:03:19,013
So we need to forward this to send as well,

79
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:21,357
or pass this information to send as well.

80
00:03:23,142 --> 00:03:24,452
And as a last argument,

81
00:03:24,986 --> 00:03:25,536
optionally,

82
00:03:26,134 --> 00:03:29,336
we can pass in an object where we provide

83
00:03:29,369 --> 00:03:30,841
extra information to send.

84
00:03:31,779 --> 00:03:33,735
For example, whether the response should be

85
00:03:33,735 --> 00:03:35,997
gzipped, so if it should be minified to be

86
00:03:35,997 --> 00:03:36,369
smaller.

87
00:03:37,237 --> 00:03:40,448
Or what our root folder is in which we wanna

88
00:03:40,448 --> 00:03:42,857
look. By default, it takes the root folder

89
00:03:42,937 --> 00:03:44,109
of this application,

90
00:03:44,639 --> 00:03:47,272
but if your static files are stored in a

91
00:03:47,272 --> 00:03:49,327
different folder, something we'll do in a

92
00:03:49,375 --> 00:03:51,672
second, then you should specify a root

93
00:03:51,688 --> 00:03:52,025
folder.

94
00:03:52,731 --> 00:03:54,273
For the moment, we don't need it.

95
00:03:54,995 --> 00:03:57,837
Now, by adding this middleware, we enable

96
00:03:57,885 --> 00:04:01,177
the browser to fetch static resources like

97
00:04:01,177 --> 00:04:02,028
CSS files.

98
00:04:03,327 --> 00:04:04,993
Now, if we would leave it like this, it

99
00:04:05,089 --> 00:04:05,987
wouldn't work though

100
00:04:06,531 --> 00:04:08,742
because this middleware would run before our

101
00:04:08,935 --> 00:04:11,450
route functions and essentially that means

102
00:04:11,514 --> 00:04:12,107
that all

103
00:04:12,716 --> 00:04:15,488
incoming requests would be treated as

104
00:04:15,584 --> 00:04:17,731
requests for static resources

105
00:04:18,308 --> 00:04:20,791
and we would try to send back such a, well,

106
00:04:20,807 --> 00:04:22,938
static resource. And of course, for all

107
00:04:23,067 --> 00:04:25,278
those requests that normally would be

108
00:04:25,278 --> 00:04:28,178
handled by our routes, we won't find such a

109
00:04:28,178 --> 00:04:30,165
static resource. There is no addGoal

110
00:04:30,181 --> 00:04:31,831
function. File, for example.

111
00:04:32,744 --> 00:04:35,661
Therefore, this should go after our routes

112
00:04:35,885 --> 00:04:38,897
so that our routes can kick in first and can

113
00:04:38,897 --> 00:04:41,814
try to handle the request first. And only if

114
00:04:41,942 --> 00:04:43,352
our routes fail

115
00:04:43,881 --> 00:04:45,900
and there is no route defined for the

116
00:04:45,964 --> 00:04:49,056
requested resource, this middleware kicks in

117
00:04:49,473 --> 00:04:50,546
and will help us out.

118
00:04:51,171 --> 00:04:53,847
In addition, I mentioned that send returns a

119
00:04:53,895 --> 00:04:54,408
promise

120
00:04:55,321 --> 00:04:57,709
and we should await that promise.

121
00:04:59,024 --> 00:05:01,159
Because what send does ultimately is

122
00:05:01,753 --> 00:05:04,529
it does not send back a response. Instead,

123
00:05:04,577 --> 00:05:07,852
it manipulates this response object on the

124
00:05:07,852 --> 00:05:10,099
context. That's why we're passing the

125
00:05:10,099 --> 00:05:11,399
context to send,

126
00:05:12,169 --> 00:05:14,512
and we need to wait for its manipulation to

127
00:05:14,512 --> 00:05:17,257
finish. If we don't await here, we're

128
00:05:17,385 --> 00:05:20,274
basically saying to Oak that we're fine and

129
00:05:20,274 --> 00:05:22,649
the response can be sent as soon as this

130
00:05:22,762 --> 00:05:25,764
line was executed. Not when all the actions

131
00:05:25,924 --> 00:05:28,044
started by that finished, but simply when

132
00:05:28,236 --> 00:05:29,970
this send function was

133
00:05:30,548 --> 00:05:33,037
executed, when the execution of send started

134
00:05:33,037 --> 00:05:33,744
to be precise.

135
00:05:34,418 --> 00:05:36,730
And that's of course too early. We don't

136
00:05:36,811 --> 00:05:39,075
wanna send back a response just because we

137
00:05:39,075 --> 00:05:42,896
started this send process. We wanna await

138
00:05:42,928 --> 00:05:46,156
for this because ultimately send manipulates

139
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:48,676
the response and we wanna give send the time

140
00:05:48,709 --> 00:05:49,351
to do so.

141
00:05:49,897 --> 00:05:51,230
And it tells us once it's done

142
00:05:51,761 --> 00:05:53,158
with this promise here.

143
00:05:53,689 --> 00:05:55,617
That's why we await the promise. This

144
00:05:55,617 --> 00:05:58,412
ensures that we wait until send is done, and

145
00:05:58,428 --> 00:06:01,561
only then we inform Oak that we are done

146
00:06:01,561 --> 00:06:03,955
with this middleware, and hence the response

147
00:06:04,036 --> 00:06:05,707
may be sent back to the client.

148
00:06:06,365 --> 00:06:08,695
Once we do all of that and we reload, we

149
00:06:08,695 --> 00:06:11,025
should see this, which definitely looks

150
00:06:11,041 --> 00:06:11,507
nicer.

151
00:06:12,085 --> 00:06:14,254
Not perfect though, and the simple reason

152
00:06:14,254 --> 00:06:17,441
for that is that I added one rule here in

153
00:06:17,474 --> 00:06:20,603
the CSS file that needs an ID being added,

154
00:06:21,103 --> 00:06:23,491
and it needs an ID being added on this div.

155
00:06:23,781 --> 00:06:25,895
So make sure that on this div you add the

156
00:06:26,008 --> 00:06:28,043
add-goal-form ID.

157
00:06:30,384 --> 00:06:32,952
And if you do that and reload, now you have

158
00:06:32,952 --> 00:06:33,969
that nicer look here.

159
00:06:36,183 --> 00:06:38,600
So this is how you can send back static

160
00:06:38,664 --> 00:06:41,226
resources, and this will work for all CSS

161
00:06:41,339 --> 00:06:43,965
files, all JavaScript files, and all images

162
00:06:43,997 --> 00:06:44,529
you might have.

163
00:06:45,324 --> 00:06:49,000
We basically use send to let Oak manipulate

164
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:52,227
the response through the context object, and

165
00:06:52,291 --> 00:06:53,768
we wait until it's done with this

166
00:06:53,816 --> 00:06:54,442
manipulation.

167
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:57,059
And we also let it know for which kind of

168
00:06:57,059 --> 00:06:59,692
request, for which requested resource, it

169
00:06:59,692 --> 00:07:00,944
should do this manipulation.

170
00:07:01,763 --> 00:07:03,754
As I mentioned, it is important that you do

171
00:07:03,770 --> 00:07:06,322
this after your routes were processed,

172
00:07:06,675 --> 00:07:08,682
because if you do it before the routes are

173
00:07:08,682 --> 00:07:11,042
processed, Oak will try to handle all

174
00:07:11,492 --> 00:07:13,812
incoming requests with this middleware, and

175
00:07:13,828 --> 00:07:16,228
that's not what we want. We only wanna

176
00:07:16,228 --> 00:07:18,677
handle the requests that are not handled by

177
00:07:18,677 --> 00:07:21,078
the routes because that will typically be

178
00:07:21,078 --> 00:07:23,913
the requests that are reaching out to static

179
00:07:23,978 --> 00:07:24,590
resources.
